This endpoint retrieves all runtime incidents for the provided customer GUID.
You can optionally include filters in the request body.

### Ticketing filters (MVP)

Runtime incidents may include an `attributes.hasTicket` boolean.
You can filter incidents by ticket presence using:

```json
{
"filters": {
"hasTicket": true
}
}
```

Use `false` to retrieve incidents without tickets.

## Path params
`provider` - required. Provider of the siem integration.
There are 4 providers:
sumoLogic
splunk
microsoftSentinel
webhook

## Query params
`customerGUID` - required. Unique identifier for the customer.

## Request object
The request body contains details about the siem integration to be created.

### Request object examples
Create a siem integration for Microsoft Sentinel:
```json
{
"name": "Microsoft Sentinel SIEM Integration",
"configuration": {
"workSpaceID": "1234567",
"primaryKey": "14rwetge6253456"
},
}
```

Create a siem integration for Sumo Logic:
```json
{
"name": "Sumo Logic SIEM Integration",
"configuration": {
"httpSourceAddress": "https://endpointX.collection.<region>.sumologic.com/receiver/v1/http/<token>"
},
}
```

Create a siem integration for Splunk:
```json
{
"name": "Splunk SIEM Integration",
"configuration": {
"url": "https://http-inputs-your_instance_name.splunkcloud.com",
"port": "8080",
"token": "some_token"
},
}
```

Create a siem integration for Webhook:
headers is optional.
```json
{
"name": "Webhook SIEM Integration",
"configuration": {
"webhookURL": "some_webhookURL",
"headers": {
"some_header": "some_value"
}
}
}
```

